  "method": "Native CPU cell updates of the constructed static graph, with explicit local phase/connectivity/fatigue assumptions. Foot fixture follows neural flexion/extension outputs; it is not Webots physics. Neural states and motor outputs are never injected.",
  "stimuli": "STOP at step 10, one START at 100 except standing, final STOP at steps-100. Foot becomes airborne on knee flexion, lands after at least 18 fixture steps when extension appears. The longer 1800-step baseline run used STOP at 1650. Restart also STOP450/START650. Left tilt at500..699.",
  "limitations": [
    "No device runtime or Webots run.",
    "Static weights only; no STDP3 update validation.",
    "No claim that harness steps map to body milliseconds.",
    "Two opposed knee-output frames occur during the final STOP transition in restart; all output paths subsequently clear. The adapter cancels opposing commands."
  ],
